# Optional deploy inputs for `npm run deploy`
#
# Localhost development uses `.dev.vars` plus `wrangler.dev.jsonc`, not this file.
# Put local model auth like `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or
# `OPENAI_API_KEY` in `.dev.vars`.
# Leave these unset to use the public workers.dev bootstrap flow.
# Set the first three to deploy directly to a protected custom domain.
# The hostname must be an exact host that Tiller owns. It can be either:
# - an apex domain like `example.com`
# - a subdomain like `tiller.example.com`
# It must not already be covered by a wildcard Cloudflare Access app.
# The Cloudflare token should start from `Edit Cloudflare Workers`, then add:
# Account / Access: Apps and Policies / Edit
# Account / Access: Service Tokens / Edit (if your dashboard exposes it)

TILLER_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=tiller.example.com
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
TILLER_ACCESS_EMAILS=you@example.com,teammate@example.com

# Not required for deploys. Only set these if you also want to run the local
# `tiller` client against the protected hub.
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=
